{"id": "EUVD-2026-103578", "enisaUuid": "9e20ee39-bd34-3c80-8d7a-76b9f3c833b5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipe: protect the dm-verity root hash with RCU\n\nipe_bdev_setintegrity() frees the old root hash when dm-verity publishes\na new one on ->preresume, while policy evaluation can still be\ndereferencing it.\n\nProtect the root hash with RCU. The evaluation path already runs under\nrcu_read_lock().\n\n[FW: remove model name according to latest guideline]", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:17:51", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:21:16", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3bd335ed62444bec61201df7d368a0779e5bd300", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/599d0498a39319285afa908762e0c9fad29f772e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d7c5bd3159235edb0f2febe2cd3d3b0fb53986f1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2776e9c28513a1c855a94792b292cbcc533418c8"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8f5g-gpf2-m64q", "CVE-2026-98533"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "10dcf95c-d87d-33eb-bb69-4b9ebdcdeef9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12"}, {"id": "2a704219-b8eb-3b63-a205-8a0359b9ec4f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e155858dd99523d4afe0f74e9c26e4f4499eb5af <3bd335ed62444bec61201df7d368a0779e5bd300"}, {"id": "2f195f92-06fd-375c-a422-68fd8df23e6c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e155858dd99523d4afe0f74e9c26e4f4499eb5af <599d0498a39319285afa908762e0c9fad29f772e"}, {"id": "79c1c96d-d08f-3726-bd5a-80ba9bb38901", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "a3890628-a430-334e-8765-e69ecbee5938", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "b8d465ba-ef3b-32f0-a205-c5942ef50fbe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "produc